  <p>Fuel types represented in the data are:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>E10</strong> — Standard unleaded petrol (95 RON, up to 10% ethanol), the default grade at most UK pumps since 2021.</li>
    <li><strong>B7_STANDARD</strong> — Standard diesel (containing up to 7% biodiesel), the most common diesel grade.</li>
    <li><strong>E5</strong> — Super unleaded petrol (97+ RON, up to 5% ethanol), a premium petrol option.</li>
    <li><strong>B7_PREMIUM</strong> — Premium diesel grade, typically higher cetane with enhanced additive packages.</li>
    <li><strong>B10</strong> — Diesel with up to 10% biodiesel content, a higher-blend renewable diesel option.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>No missing values were detected across any of the six columns. Station metadata (brand, address, coordinates) is not included in this dataset, limiting geographic and brand-level analysis.</p>

