'''

html += f'''    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <p><strong>Policy-relevant findings:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>{highest_spread['fuel_type']}</strong> shows the widest price spread at <strong>{highest_spread['price_spread']:.1f}p/L</strong>. A motorist filling a typical 55-litre tank could pay up to <strong>£{(highest_spread['price_spread'] * 55 / 100):.2f}</strong> more at the most expensive station versus the cheapest — a significant consumer impact.</li>
    <li>The interquartile range for <strong>{highest_iqr['fuel_type']}</strong> is <strong>{highest_iqr['iqr']:.1f}p/L</strong>, meaning even the middle 50% of stations show meaningful price variation of <strong>£{(highest_iqr['iqr'] * 55 / 100):.2f}</strong> on a typical tank fill.</li>
