  <p>The timeliness with which retailers update their reported prices is both a measure of data quality and an indicator of retailer compliance with the government's open data scheme. The lag between <code>source_updated_at</code> (when the retailer reported the price) and <code>recorded_at</code> (when the data was captured) reveals how fresh or stale reported prices are.</p>

